  "body": "Found while gating #237 (PR from fork branch `issue/237-wide-class-bins`), and reproduced on `origin/main` at c9a9fb3 with the same message and line, so it is not caused by that branch.\n\n**Failing test (debug, Linux):** `cargo test -p camcraft-motion --test rotary_dflat -- a_d_flat_bar_wraps_in_every_placement`\n\n```\npanicked at crates/motion/tests/rotary_dflat.rs:183:27:\nthrough flat at phi 0: invalid machining parameters: the model's normals share no rotation axis - a turned workpiece is rotary work; finish a freeform with the 5-Axis kinds\n```\n\nThe other three `rotary_dflat` tests pass. The refusal is the axis fit's \"share no rotation axis\", not #226's seam refusal: the D-flat bar placed with its flat \"through\" at phi 0 no longer fits an axis at all. Likely from one of the recent axis-fit merges (#223 / #208 point-concurrency, #116 band) - not bisected.\n\nNot a gouge (a refusal, fails closed) but main is red, so P1.\n\nDone means: the through-flat placement fits its axis again (or the test's expectation is changed with a reason), and `rotary_dflat` is green on main.\n",
